   1634  fafe							; ========================================================================
   1635  fafe							; BombMarkWalls (S5.2, moved from bank0) — pinned at $FB10.
   1636  fafe							;   On the bomb 1->2 edge: walk the rect cache, set WallMask bit (BombPacked
   1637  fafe							;   b3-6) for each w==2 rect whose x is in blast cols (bomb left-half col
   1638  fafe							;   +-2, clamped 0..19). w==2 = one D7 logical cell (rect x/w are emitted
   1639  fafe							;   in 4px display cols; a thin wall is exactly one cell = 2 cols). Skip x==0 (screen border). Score is NOT done here —
   1640  fafe							;   pads cannot nest (ReturnPad switches to bank0), so this returns
   1641  fafe							;   A = #walls newly broken and the bank0 caller adds +75 per wall.
   1642  fafe							;   Plan 5.1: each newly broken rect is punched here immediately —
   1643  fafe							;   ClearPFColumn on col x AND col x+1 (D7 thin wall w = 2 display cols;
   1644  fafe							;   the single-col punch left half the wall standing behind a set mask bit)
   1645  fafe							;   — the old VBL ApplyBombWalls re-apply + EnterRoom
   1646  fafe							;   restore are deleted (D1-B). WallMask b3-6 survives only in-room: the
   1647  fafe							;   hot parent-mask AND (HotOverlapBody) still reads it until phase 6.
   1648  fafe							;   ABW tables + BombMaskBit are bank1-only now (kernel copies died with
   1649  fafe							;   ApplyBombWalls).
   1650  fafe							;   #7(i): walk now covers rects 0-4 (cache slot rect4 at $DC-$DF was
   1651  fafe							;   loaded but never walked — a thin wall there was unbreakable). Rect5
   1652  fafe							;   is not cached (ZP ends $DF) and stays unwalkable — shipped models
   1653  fafe							;   have no thin rect at idx5. Rect idx4 has no WallMask bit: PairGone's
   1654  fafe							;   buffer read replaces the mask as its double-score guard. A full
   1655  fafe							;   buffer cell-sweep was evaluated and REJECTED: find_rectangles merges
   1656  fafe							;   maximal runs, so every shipped thin wall has a solid neighbor slab
   1657  fafe							;   (checked all 8 models) — buffer adjacency cannot distinguish thin
   1658  fafe							;   stubs from thick walls without breaking gameplay parity.
   1659  fafe							;   Also fixed: the col x+1 punch passed the ABW table VALUE (the rect's
   1660  fafe							;   ZP address) as the ClearPFColumn col instead of deref'ing rect.x —
   1661  fafe							;   the second half of every thin wall was punched at a garbage col
   1662  fafe							;   (caught by the new test_bomb_strip rect-walk case; pre-existing
   1663  fafe							;   since plan 5.1). RcBase is now clamped ≤5 at the bank2 cache load —
   1664  fafe							;   BMW trusts it (no local clamp).
   1665  fafe							; ========================================================================
   1666  fafe		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FB10 - *, 0
   1667  fb10				   BombMarkWalls
   1668  fb10							; visible-left mapping identical to PlayerHitsMap: the bomb is drawn from
   1669  fb10							; BombX via SetObjectXPos, so its left edge is BombX-5 / BombX-7, not BombX.
   1670  fb10		       38		      sec
   1671  fb11		       a5 f6		      lda	BombX
   1672  fb13		       c9 0f		      cmp	#15
   1673  fb15		       90 04		      bcc	.BMWoff7
   1674  fb17		       e9 07		      sbc	#7	; visible left = BombX - 7
   1675  fb19		       b0 02		      bcs	.BMWVL	; C set (X>=15) — skip the -5 path
   1676  fb1b				   .BMWoff7
   1677  fb1b		       e9 04		      sbc	#4	; visible left = BombX - 5 (CMP clears carry)
   1678  fb1d				   .BMWVL
   1679  fb1d		       4a		      lsr
   1680  fb1e		       4a		      lsr		; screen col = visible_left/4 (0..39)
   1681  fb1f		       85 92		      sta	RectCount	; ORIGINAL screen col (0..39): >=20 = right
   1682  fb21							; bomb → real blast lives in the right half,
   1683  fb21							; so M1StripBlast must skip its left overlap
   1684  fb21							; test (the window below is mirror-space for
